    "done_when": "Design how a lane becomes a subscription with a model chosen inside it, ready for the lead to approve and to build in nodes.\n\nThe lead's direction, 2026-10-07: it should be possible to specify a lane and a model within it, and claude-opus should not exist as its own lane, because it duplicates claude. Today every model is its own backend name in both families:\n- codex (gpt-6-sol), codex-astra and codex-luna, joined only by budget_group codex-sub in docs/state/reckon/model-catalogue.yaml;\n- claude (sonnet 5.5), claude-opus and claude-haiku, each a full backend block in the host flight (dotfiles reckon/flight.yaml) with identical launch config.\nRosters, the ledger, review_excluded_backends, budget groups and the picker's candidates all key on those backend names.\n\nProduce the design as /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/lane-and-model-design/report.md, answering:\n1. Schema. How flight and the catalogue declare one lane per subscription or host (claude, codex, clive) with its models, a default model and per-model effort and rates. Name the exact keys, and how the existing --set override reaches a model within a lane.\n2. Dispatch surface. How a caller names a lane and a model (for example --backend claude --model opus), and how --local and the \"a named lane is authoritative\" rule extend to a named model.\n3. Picker. Whether Jev's candidates become lane-and-model pairs or a lane followed by a model choice. How subscription pace is pooled per lane while model fit differs. What the question template must say.\n4. History. How existing ledger rows, rosters, review records and budget groups keyed on codex-astra, codex-luna, claude-opus and claude-haiku read after the change, with old names becoming aliases so no committed row is rewritten.\n5. Migration order, as a sequence of independently landable nodes with their write paths and gates. Say which node retires the claude-opus backend block.\n6. The call-site census behind each answer: grep counts by file for each backend name and for budget_group, so the scope is measured rather than guessed.\nWrite only that report and the raw census beside it; change nothing in the repository. The coordinator lands the evidence.",
    "estimated_hours": null,
